art (absent new rules in ATYON).</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;When her Blood Potency falls below six dots, the vampire does not lose<br /> any Attributes or Skills above the fifth dot.&quot; (VtR 2nd ed., p.89)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T19:20:18-07:00","id":866215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/824600-vtr-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=866182#post866182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I bring life to this thread.<br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/vampire-the-requiem-baby-youre-much-too-fast/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/vampire-the-r...much-too-fast/</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I like where this is heading.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T20:45:58-07:00","id":866237,"title":"","content":"I like the mention of how elders are also going to get specialized rituals and coils and such, that's interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/themes/stvault/images/affiliatebanner4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Christopher%20Falco&amp;affiliate_id=259490\" target=\"_blank\">Storytellers' Vault supplements (WoD, CoD)</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/FalconianP\" target=\"_blank\">My Patreon! (CofD bonuses include: Fae Sorcery/Technomancy for Vampires, Quick Conversion for Inferno, and more!)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1130-falco1029","name":"falco1029","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1130_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1045"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-15T20:47:17-07:00","id":866239,"title":"","content":"Rules for flashback scenes make Mummy very happy. And crossover antagonists? Oh boy!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T02:22:48-07:00","id":866322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stylanski</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/824600-vtr-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=866201#post866201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;When her Blood Potency falls below six dots, the vampire does not lose<br /> any Attributes or Skills above the fifth dot.&quot; (VtR 2nd ed., p.89)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Exactly. Thanks Stylanski <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> This is one of the changes of 2ed that I like more <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T04:32:36-07:00","id":866339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Marcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/824600-vtr-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=866322#post866322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Exactly. Thanks Stylanski <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> This is one of the changes of 2ed that I like more <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>You're welcome. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Apart from the fact that this whole outline looks awesome, the bits about Lost Clans especially peeked my interest. I'm currently finishing the Preludes in a modern Athens chronicle, where the main plot point is a slumbering ancient and one of the Vrihi bloodline/clan.<br /> <br /> The Vrihi were clearly intended as a nod to the Brujah and True Brujah of VtM. It all started with my gripe with clan names in VtM and how ahistorical they were. So I came up with the Vrihi (Those Who Roar in ancient Greek), a clan of Philosopher Kings that fled demonic entities from either the Middle East or lower Egypt, and rose alongside the classical Greek civilization (if not directly influencing its emergence). Their weakness? Tragic and awesome. Though they struggled to be detached, scholarly and just rulers, their use of the Beast gave them the ability to influence the general aura of politics in their city states, similar to how feeding grounds get influenced by the Kindred who hunt there. The weakness meant that this tie could become uncontrollable, and in the event of strong and negative experienced emotions (such as Frenzy etc.), that would ooze to the mortals who surrounded them and threaten to ruin the political structures they worked so hard to establish.<br /> <br /> If the Vrihi ancient were to rise, she would discover that her clan now mystically resembles more of a bloodline.<br /> <br /> The chronicle is set to take place during June 2015, the time of the Greek referendum. I do not intend to use the Vrihi is the driving point behind every major event in Greek politics. But the powers and weakness described above, definitely heightened certain pre-existing trends in politics and the people. She's not the reason people disagree, but she might be the reason why people and the country's rulers disagree so passionately.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":59,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","user":"stylanski","date":". 04-16-2016, 08:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T11:22:26-07:00","id":866460,"title":"","content":"I'm minorly (very minorly) disappointed that we aren't getting any more signature settings now that we know The Pack will include new Hunting Grounds. This would be a perfect time to see what a city with a storied history, like London, Paris, Kiev, Istanbul, or even Rome itself looks like in modern night, and how the Elders play a role in those settings.<br /> <br /> Otherwise though, this looks like it will be awesome! I can't wait!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T11:32:19-07:00","id":866462,"title":"","content":"A Guide to Night seems like another likely place to put settings, should Rose and Danielle have an interest in that.<br /> <br /> EDIT: That said, one thing that's observable in a lot of Vampire's books is the tendency to 'hint' at settings, which can provide some good fodder. Observe the mention of Seoul in the Lancea et Sanctum write up, or how David A. Hill has mentioned the New York Domain gets some detail second-hand in <i>Secrets of the Covenants</i>. (I feel like it's also worth pointing out that it is also given some detail in the Daeva Clanbook)<br /> <br /> I'd also bet good money that London's story is the same as it was in Shadows of the UK, if <i>Requiem for Regina </i>is anything to go by.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 04-16-2016, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T11:51:10-07:00","id":866472,"title":"","content":"more about ghoul families? Methuselah? surviving members of Lost Clans? Inamorata and other horrors? crossovers with similarly ancient beings? [REDACTED]?! I love all of this. Now, excuse me, but I'm going to check every vampire book I have for page 63 :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-16T11:58:28-07:00","id":866477,"title":"","content":"Stew said he liked the idea of putting more Hunting Grounds in the Pack, but it doesn't seem to be something that's a rule across all gamelines.<br /> <br /> The p63 reference seems to be of the Inamorata, from the Daeva clan book. Unsure about the other [REDACTED]s and wonder if some refer to a gameline to come.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T10:16:06-07:00","id":866904,"title":"","content":"This looks great!<br /> <br /> Wel exept four teh fact that I am reminded off a pet peeve of mine, that anonymus asholes in the XVII century coldnt evan stale worlds preperly.<br /> <br /> Inamorata, with one &quot;N&quot;. tsk.<br /> <br /> (I bet I managed to convey my feelings on the matter with that sentence...)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1866-ophion","name":"Ophion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T13:52:28-07:00","id":867034,"title":"","content":"Has it ever been explained why the Fog of Ages went away in 2e?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T15:30:55-07:00","id":867110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/824600-vtr-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=867034#post867034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has it ever been explained why the Fog of Ages went away in 2e?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that I can recall. Probably because it still happens on occasion, thus allowing STs to use it for any chronicles that need it as a plot hook while giving others the option to explore Kindred history. Vampires still lie about their history anyway, the fog felt like a mechanics intrusion directed at something Masquerade did over the top.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T15:41:03-07:00","id":867121,"title":"","content":"I'm very grateful that fog of eternity is no longer a mechanics. I like the idea that immortal being can remember, more or less, the story they live.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T16:20:44-07:00","id":867141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/824600-vtr-a-thousand-years-of-night?p=867034#post867034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has it ever been explained why the Fog of Ages went away in 2e?</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically they leave it up to you. Some people like it and think it is cool others do not. I thought it was a great way to explain why the player got something wrong when referred to their characters past.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T19:24:00-07:00","id":867290,"title":"","content":"Rose wrote a post about it awhile back, when <i>Blood &amp; Smoke </i>first came out. If you look at the themes of Requiem, the Fog of Ages doesn't really do anything to serve them as a standard incident (note, Vampires still can go into torpor and lose memories, as the 2e core notes, but this does not happen as a standard.) In the original core, it was written in support of the idea of elders and Kindred writ large as static beings, unable to adapt with the times.<br /> <br /> This was definitely an artifact from Masquerade, and a component of the punkishness of the prior game transferring over. It wasn't needed any longer and conflicted with the new presentation of elders, which highlights in a consistent fashion that these are old beings with powerful abilities, resources cultivated over centuries and the capacity to live a thousand different lives over the course of their Requiem.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the thing to keep in mind is that the Fog of Ages was <i>also </i>introduced because the original team had it in their head that the only way to keep the history of the Kindred vague was to fuck with their memory. Thankfully, Rose and company realized that doesn't need to be the case. Individual Kindred lie, have motivations for presenting events certain ways, and often distort each other's ideas over the centuries. Institutions like the Sanctified burn histories they don't really like, and other forces like competing Covenants, the Strix and the attrition rate for the Kindred present make the idea of assembling a complete or correct history a difficult task.<br /> <br /> So again, it's not the norm, but it still can occur. It just wasn't as interesting as making the narrative unreliable through an external everpresent factor like the Fog of Ages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 04-17-2016, 10:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T02:48:27-07:00","id":867455,"title":"","content":"I actually really like that the best option for an Elder that is, in fact, seriously losing touch with humanity and the times, bereft of touchstones and annoyed and bored both by the current zeitgeist... is actually to go to sleep and wake up next century all refreshed and ready to interact with the new environment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/7019410/Images/Ex3%20KS%20Badge.gif\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1866-ophion","name":"Ophion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T04:57:24-07:00","id":867490,"title":"","content":"Let's not forget.... People forget shit by themselves, they don't need a magical force doing it for them <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-18T11:55:10-07:00","id":867710,"title":"","content":"something I've thought about for the third [REDACTED] at Wolves at the Gate.<br /> <br /> That section talks about crossover with ancient supernaturals. The fact it is redacted means it is not Mummy or something obvious like that. Considering we don't even know Deviant's title, I don't think it comes from that direction. Considering we know a lot about Changeling, I don't think it comes from that direction either. That may mean it could be something that most people just won't think about, and could come as a surprise, something old and long lived that just doesn't take that much room in the setting.. like the Purified.<br /> <br /> (please be it the purified, pretty please with sugar on top!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?au